A||||4||Homicidal||Clutch won't DEPRESS?  Can't shift at all!!!!!!||||8||
Z||000000||Homicidal||04-19-2000||02:32 AM||||I was coming back from LA down to San Diego (where else!) when I hit some traffic and had to slow down.  I downshifted to first since I had to stop and started off again, but when I shifted into 3rd gear my clutch stuck a little and the gears grinded.  When I finally got into 3rd my clutch pedal locked up and I couldn't press it down to shift anymore!  I managed to get across 3-4 lanes and get off the freeway into a parking lot.<P>Now my car won't start because I cannot press the clutch down to make it start!  It's like it has a brick underneath it or something!  What's wrong with my car?  Why did it lock up so quickly and suddenly?||||reg||8
Z||000001||Carrolles||04-19-2000||07:22 AM||||It sounds like the throw out bearing is binding on the shaft.  This is internal to the bell housing and requires separating the transmission from the engine to replace.<P>First look at the cheaper easier areas.  The clutch master cylinder is actuated by a shaft that is connected to the clutch pedal.  I believe there is a snap ring that keeps this shaft from pulling out of the master cylinder.  If this snap ring has come loose the shaft could be jammed in the opening of the master cylinder causing the pedal to be stuck in the up position.  Replacing/rebuilding the clutch master cylinder is far easier than replacing the throw out bearing.<P>Also look for similar problems at the clutch slave cylinder.<P>Hope this helps,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||04-19-2000||09:28 AM||||Along Carrolles' line of reasoning a quick check to see if the problem is in the hydraulic system or not would be to open the bleeder screw on the slave and then see if you can push the clutch down.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroshop||04-19-2000||12:06 PM||||I ahve had several cars come or towed to my shop and it has been a bad throwout bearing or a busted input shaft seal and bearing. This seal has a a small pipe that comes out of the seal and bearing and the throwout bearing slides on it. If that breaks then you have to open the gear box to replace it. It means you have to pull the tranny and open the trnny case just so you can replace the bearing. You can see what the bearing looks like on my online parts catalog.<BR>Sorry I just looked on my web site and the bearing is not on there as yet.<p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 04-19-2000).]||||reg||9
Z||000004||Oreif||04-19-2000||12:26 PM||||I've heard that some aftermarket throw-out bearings have bigger tolerences that original GM spec. Especially the B&M bearing. They have a tendancy to jam up over the lip on the shaft and cause the problem your seeing. I've heard of this more so with the getreg 5spd.||||reg||1
